# Normalize line endings so Windows lab machines and macOS agree.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.py   text
*.md   text
*.html text
*.json text

# Binaries. Marked so git stops trying to diff or merge them.
*.jpg  binary
*.png  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.zip  binary

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Git LFS: deliberately NOT used in this repo. Read this before adding it.
#
# GitHub Pages does not serve LFS-tracked files. It serves the pointer file
# instead, so an <img> tag or a Miro image widget receives about 130 bytes of
# ASCII rather than a JPEG. Tracking idea-wall/slides/ in LFS silently breaks
# the wall, and it breaks it in the worst possible place: on a classroom TV,
# with no error anywhere in git.
#
# Source: "Git LFS cannot be used with GitHub Pages sites."
# https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/working-with-files/managing-large-files/about-git-large-file-storage
#
# The published slides do not need LFS anyway. 66 JPEGs at roughly 350KB each
# is about 25MB, well inside what plain git handles comfortably.
#
# If a future subproject needs large binaries (engine content, video, builds),
# give it its own repository with LFS enabled. Do not enable LFS here and do
# not move this repo off Pages to accommodate it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
